## 8. Key Architectural Differences for Memento Design

| Aspect | DBAutoDoc (CLI) | Memento (Microservices) | Key Takeaway |
|--------|-----------------|------------------------|-------------|
| **Concurrency** | Sequential per level | Distributed via RabbitMQ | Use worker queue, not thread pools |
| **Retries** | None (fail & continue) | Implement in worker/coordinator | Dead-letter queue for persistent failures |
| **Rate Limiting** | Provider-delegated | Coordinator-side budgets | Aggregate tokens across workers before dispatch |
| **State Storage** | Single JSON file | MongoDB (coordinator writes only) | Workers stateless—all state in message payload |
| **Guardrails Check** | Before every prompt | Before dispatching task batch | Check at task-creation time, not execution |
| **Error Logging** | In-memory IterationTracker | MongoDB processing logs | Include promptInput/promptOutput in every log |
| **Template Rendering** | Nunjucks in-process | Render in worker (per-message) | Templates loaded into worker, not pre-rendered |

